# 1.0 Main Designer

## Purpose
The primary working surface where users add widgets, bind data, and position overlay elements.

## Layout anatomy
- **Header**: Title, reset/save/publish, preview launcher.
- **Tools row**: Widget palette, grid/snap/safe-zone toggles, screen size chip.
- **Canvas**: 16:9 stage with optional grid, snap, and safe-zone overlay; widgets render here.
- **Footer (metadata explorer)**: Lists fields for the selected source/endpoint and shows latest payload/test response.

## Interactions
- Click a palette card → add widget with default size/position; new widget auto-selected.
- Palette is limited to Text, Image/GIF, and Marquee while we harden the data model.
- Click canvas background → clear selection.
- Drag/resize selected widget with Moveable; snap/grid optional.
- Double-click a widget → opens Widget Editor (1.1).
- Click Preview in header → opens Preview Modal (1.2).

## Data binding surface
- Binding happens in the Widget Editor modal (source → endpoint → field → format).
- Field options come from metadata (`ApiResponseMetadata.fields`) or typed models when available.
- Bound values resolve from the virtual data dictionary (`source|endpoint` payloads), currently populated via test calls.
- Plain text overlays render without chrome; styling and template text live in the editor.

## State persistence
- Save/Publish buttons POST serialized widget list to `/designer/layout?layoutId=default` (current single layout).

## Known gaps
- No undo/redo; no multi-select.
- Grid/safe-zone are CSS only; no pixel-perfect broadcast presets yet.
- No per-project switcher; single layout id in use.



===== FILE: Docs\DesignerScreens\1.1-widget-editor-modal.md =====
# 1.1 Widget Editor Modal

## Purpose
Focused surface for configuring a widget’s data binding and layout without cluttering the canvas.

## Layout
- **Header**: Widget title, Cancel, Save.
- **Basics section**: Text content, optional “Use data source” toggle; when on, Source → Endpoint → Field → Format, Template text, Update interval, Test button.
- **Layout section**: X, Y, Width, Height numeric fields; note about drag/resize on canvas.
- **Text style section**: font size, weight, color, alignment.

## Interactions
- Open: double-click a widget on canvas.
- Live preview of the widget stays on canvas while editing; changes apply on Save.
- Cancel/backdrop closes without committing edits.
- Test button invokes `/public-api-sources/test` for the selected source/endpoint.

## Data flow
- Draft state created from the selected widget on open; merged back on Save.
- Fields are sourced from metadata or typed models; default field picks first leaf.
- Test requests also populate the virtual data dictionary so the canvas/preview can render without re-fetching.
- Template text replaces `{binding}` with the resolved field value when a data source is used; otherwise the plain text content is shown.

## Known gaps
- No undo/redo within modal; no diff/revert button beyond Cancel.
- No per-field validation beyond select presence; no type-aware formatting hints.
- No CSS/style editor yet (future enhancement for custom styles).



===== FILE: Docs\DesignerScreens\1.2-preview-modal.md =====
# 1.2 Preview Modal

## Purpose
Read-only overlay preview against motion background to judge contrast, spacing, and composition.

## Layout
- **Backdrop**: Dim/blur layer.
- **Window**: Video element (looped sample) with overlay layer on top.
- **Overlay**: Renders all current widgets with pointer-events disabled.
- **Close**: Button to dismiss (backdrop click also closes).

## Interactions
- Open via header “Preview” button on the main designer.
- View-only; no drag/resizing; no edits inside this modal.

## Data
- Uses current in-memory widget list and triggers fresh fetches for each bound source/endpoint when opened so live values appear.
- Shows same widget rendering as canvas but without selection chrome.

## Known gaps
- Uses sample video only; no per-project or per-game background yet.
- No device/aspect presets; relies on current canvas sizing CSS.
- No per-widget live data refresh trigger; depends on prior preview/test payloads.



